@baseUrl = http://localhost/pcpartsstore

### Populated list — expect 200, two seed rows
GET {{baseUrl}}/parts
Accept: application/json

### Existing part — expect 200, ID 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/parts/1
Accept: application/json

### Missing part — expect 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/parts/999999
Accept: application/json

### Brand list — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands
Accept: application/json

### Existing brand — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/brands/1
Accept: application/json

### Empty list — select isolated empty fixture first; restore normal config afterward
GET {{baseUrl}}/parts
Accept: application/json

### Users list
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Accept: application/json

### Individual user
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Accept: application/json

### Orders list
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders
Accept: application/json

### Individual order
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/1
Accept: application/json

### Create a temporary user (save returned ID; delete after demo)
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{"first_name":"Demo","last_name":"Customer","email":"demo.customer@example.com"}

### Create an order (replace user_id with the newly created user ID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"user_id":3,"status":"Processing"}
